# HTML shells and crawl files

Route `index.html` files are shells only:

```html
<html lang="nl">
  <!-- stylesheet + module script with cache query -->
  <body data-page="..." data-service="...">
    <main id="main"></main>
  </body>
</html>
```

- `data-page` required. `data-service` only on service routes, matching a `SERVICES` slug.
- Do not put page copy in the shell. Rendering happens in `assets/site.js`.
- Keep `lang="nl"`, favicon, stylesheet, and `type="module"` script.
- If `assets/site.js` or `assets/styles.css` change, bump `?v=` on every shell that loads them.

New public route: add the shell, the renderer, and a `<url>` in `sitemap.xml`. `robots.txt` should stay allow-all with the production sitemap URL.
